  "analyzed_vuln": {
    "function": "completeMolQueries",
    "file": "rdkit/Code/GraphMol/QueryOps.cpp",
    "description": "`completeMolQueries()` assumes every atom query root is an `ATOM_EQUALS_QUERY` and unconditionally downcasts `atom->getQuery()` to that derived type before passing it to `completeQueryAndChildren()`. Query roots can legitimately be composite `ATOM_AND_QUERY`/`AndQuery` objects, so this downcast is undefined behavior. The recursive helper repeats the same invalid assumption for child nodes and accesses equality-query operations (`getVal()`, `setVal()`, and the data function) through the invalid pointer. The traversal should operate on the generic atom-query base type and only treat nodes that are actually equality queries as `ATOM_EQUALS_QUERY`.",
    "conditions": "A parsed molecule must set `_NeedsQueryScan` while containing an atom whose query root is composite. In this PoV, `M  RBC  1 4  -2` creates an `AtomRingBondCount` equality-query leaf with sentinel value `0xDEADBEEF`, sets `_NeedsQueryScan`, converts atom 4 to a query atom, and AND-expands the ring-bond query with its existing atom query. `QueryAtom::expandQuery()` therefore installs an `AtomAnd` (`AndQuery`) as the root. `finishMolProcessing()` sees `_NeedsQueryScan` and calls `completeMolQueries()`, which incorrectly downcasts that `AndQuery` root to `ATOM_EQUALS_QUERY`, triggering UBSan (and potentially invalid derived-object access)."
  },
